      "message": "Please fix this WARNING reported by autoreview issue finding: By catching `IOException` here, you are double-wrapping the exception. The `IOException` thrown by `serverConfigCache.get()` currently has `ExecutionException` as its cause, so `e.getCause() instanceof RestApiException` will be false. This results in throwing `new IOException(ExecutionException)` instead of unwrapping the actual cause.\n\nInstead of catching and re-wrapping `IOException` here, you can remove this `catch` block completely and let the `IOException` from `serverConfigCache.get()` propagate. Then, unwrap the `ExecutionException` inside `ServerConfigCacheImpl` so it throws the `IOException` with the correct underlying cause.",
